EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Leinster_FedelmidAnTEigseMeasceal" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Contested Isle - Fedelmid an t-Éigse Measceal"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Core_Ext"

    # Fedelmid an t-Éigse Measceal (Chapter Six: The Province of Leinster, p65): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.

    #t71ad8262482ddc73811eec ^"Fedelmid an t-Éigse Measceal" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tbe17e73554f25eda95be4f ^"The Paruchia of Nerius"]
            ^"Age" STRING "102 (apparent age 95)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Moribund +3, Belligerent +2, Determined +1 Fedelmid (FEDGE-el-midge on TCHAY-shuh MYES-kul) was a young Céli Dé when he entered House Ex Miscellanea, or as the Irish call it t-Éigse Measceal, believing that the Order of Hermes embodied the spirit of learning and scholarship and discipline that a Gifted holy man should aspire to. He was disappointed to find many of its members did not live up to what he saw as the potential of the Order, but remains loyal to his Hermetic sodales while never for a moment betraying his primary loyalty to the Church. Yet Fedelmid’s loyalty to the Church is not of the kind that worries about dioceses, bishops or institutions, rather a personal sense of spiritual responsibility and a heroic devotion and asceticism that manifests in a saint-like life of individual spiritual aspiration."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Contested Isle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 65
        }
        DESCRIPTION "His life was changed while on pilgrimage to Rome in two ways: first, he had his strange visions in a valley while crossing the Alps that made him seek out the few who knew the secret of Saint Nerius and learn Holy Magic; and second, what he saw in Rome convinced him the Papacy may have spiritual authority but that spiritual problems are best resolved at a local level by the individuals concerned.\n\nHe took Indrechtach as an apprentice and trained him, but was saddened when he was expelled from the community at Glendalough. Now Fedelmid is a very old man, worn out with decrepitude and suffering from long Twilight episodes, and he is planning his death and burial at Qui Sonant Pro Quieto. He is planning his final leave taking from Little Saltee, but is hoping to persuade the next visitors to the covenant to escort him to Qui Sonant Pro Quieto, for in his youth he was engaged in many feuds and he still has many enemies who may end his life before he reaches there."
    }

}
